---
import ConsentState from '../components/consent-state.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/demo.astro';

const { c15t } = Astro.locals;
---

<BaseLayout title="Astro demo">
	<p>
		The banner below is server-rendered: no framework JavaScript, the same
		DOM and <code>data-testid</code>s as the Svelte and React banners, and it
		is absent from the HTML entirely once you have consented. The preference
		centre is a Svelte island that only downloads when you open it.
	</p>

	<section class="panel">
		<h2>What the server decided</h2>
		<pre>{JSON.stringify(
			{
				inputs: c15t.inputs,
				model: c15t.snapshot.model,
				policy: c15t.snapshot.policyRule.id ?? null,
				shouldShowBanner: c15t.shouldShowBanner,
			},
			null,
			2
		)}</pre>
	</section>

	<ConsentState />

	<section class="panel">
		<h2>Consent-gated inline script</h2>
		<p>
			This one is gated by its markup rather than by configuration — mark it
			inert and label it, and it runs the moment measurement consent lands.
			Gated scripts need <code>is:inline</code> so Astro ships the tag as
			written instead of bundling and running it.
		</p>
		<script data-c15t-category="measurement" is:inline type="text/plain">
			document.getElementById('inline-script-status').textContent =
				'Measurement script ran';
		</script>
		<p data-testid="inline-script-status" id="inline-script-status">
			Measurement script blocked
		</p>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
